\newlabel{tab:core_benchmark}{{II}{9}{Held-out calibration benchmark (SPOT, $q{=}10^{-3}$, held-out nominal FPR on data the threshold never saw). (a)~Retrospective buffered attribution ($S{=}64$) and (b)~strictly causal trailing attribution (zero lookahead), reported separately: non-GHL = stream-macro over 19 streams at five seeds; GHL = 14 streams at three to five seeds; DS-Macro F1 = unweighted mean of the 7 dataset means; $\Delta t$ = mean delay over detected events only. Best in \textbf {bold}, second \underline {underlined}. (c)~Per-dataset buffered results: $n$ streams, $K$ channels, anomaly prevalence $\pi $, constant-alarm reference $\text {F1}_{\text {all-pos}}{=}2\pi /(1{+}\pi )$; F1 is mean $\pm $ between-stream SD ($\pm $ seed SD for single-stream datasets). Leave-one-dataset-out ranges are given in the text. (d)~Published baselines in the 11-dataset, 130-stream single-seed panel under the same calibration protocol (Point-F1, dataset-macro / stream mean)}{table.2}{}}
