\newlabel{tab:operating_and_horizon}{{III}{11}{(a) Target-horizon and score-emission sweep on five streams at three seeds ($S$ = target horizon; lag $= S{-}1$ steps before a score can be emitted; held-out FPR and event recall (ER) under strictly causal trailing attribution, with buffered OpEntropy FPR/ER for contrast; $\Delta t$ = mean delay over detected events). (b) Detection quality at matched nominal calibration budgets $q^*$ on 19 non-GHL streams (stream-averaged; ER = event recall; P = point precision; FA = false alarms per 1{,}000 nominal steps). Budgets match calibration quantiles, not realized test FPR}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces (a) Calibrator comparison on identical score streams (33 streams, cell-weighted means with stream-macro in parentheses; up to five seeds). Design risk $q{=}10^{-3}{=}0.1\%$. Overshoot $>q$ is the share of cells whose 95\% CI lower bound exceeds $q=10^{-3}$. Buffered smear inflates FPR by painting alarms over $S=64$ steps; causal trailing reflects strict step-level alarms. (b) Controlled-drift stress test: achieved held-out FPR (design $q=10^{-3}$) of real held-out residual streams under injected shifts, averaged over 16 streams with $\ge 200$ calibration and evaluation windows. Rolling variants recalibrate per evaluation block.}}{11}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:calibrator_comparison}{{IV}{11}{(a) Calibrator comparison on identical score streams (33 streams, cell-weighted means with stream-macro in parentheses; up to five seeds). Design risk $q{=}10^{-3}{=}0.1\%$. Overshoot $>q$ is the share of cells whose 95\% CI lower bound exceeds $q=10^{-3}$. Buffered smear inflates FPR by painting alarms over $S=64$ steps; causal trailing reflects strict step-level alarms. (b) Controlled-drift stress test: achieved held-out FPR (design $q=10^{-3}$) of real held-out residual streams under injected shifts, averaged over 16 streams with $\ge 200$ calibration and evaluation windows. Rolling variants recalibrate per evaluation block}{table.4}{}}
